From: EglantinePS5 <Vampinity@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: up: guard held write age, writes held for a guard already lifted are applied (EDEN_UP_AHEAD_GUARD_HELD_AGE)

DRAFT, not built. Our own work (guard-door job). With EDEN_UP_AHEAD_GUARD=3 at boot. Gated by
EDEN_UP_AHEAD_GUARD_HELD_AGE (exact 1, live, Id AheadGuardHeldAge, not armed); off by default.
On: each held guest write is tagged with the guard it was held for, and a gather while a newer
guard is up applies the writes (and redirty ranges) whose guard is lifted, unless the current
guard has a copy of the page. EDEN_UP_AHEAD_GUARD_HELD_AGE_VERIFY (exact 1, live, Id
AheadGuardHeldAgeVerify) only counts what it would apply early. The live-switch start warns when
either is used without EDEN_UP_AHEAD_GUARD=3. 10 s line names applied/early counts.

Reviewed draft (verdict "ready with corrections"): guard-held-write-age.v2.patch. live_switch.h
re-anchored after AheadReadSync; gpu.cpp's `#include "common/live_switch.h"` is now a repeat of
0567's (kept as the draft has it); all +/- lines byte-identical to the v2.
---
diff --git a/src/common/live_switch.h b/src/common/live_switch.h
